# What is never sent to Vercel (a `vercel deploy` from your computer uploads the folder as it is).
# Keeps the upload under Vercel's size limit and keeps private material and secrets off Vercel.
# The function's own bundle is trimmed separately ("excludeFiles" in vercel.json).

# Fundraising, demo-making and generated reports: not part of the product. (A leading / means
# "at the top of the repository only": frontend/public/sdk, for example, is part of the website.)
/deck
/memory
/.demovideo
/test_reports
/.emergent
/.github
/.gitconfig
/sdk
**/*.md

# Installed and built by Vercel itself
**/node_modules
frontend/build
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv
**/venv
# Left by a local `vercel build`; uploaded, they would replace api/requirements.txt as the package list
api/pyproject.toml
api/uv.lock

# Tests run in CI, not on Vercel
/tests
backend/tests

# Anything that could hold a secret
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
.vercel

# Investor material is not published. To publish it from the website, delete these three lines
# AND set SERVE_INVESTOR_DOCS=true in the project's environment variables, then redeploy.
frontend/public/docs/vexen-pitch-deck.pdf
frontend/public/docs/vexen-cap-table.pdf
frontend/public/docs/vexen-idea-one-pager.pdf
